fbterm-compat.patch -- xterm sequences + alternate screen for FbTerm 1.7
========================================================================

Stock FbTerm 1.7 (Debian fbterm 1.7-5) lacks: bright SGR
(90-97/100-107), 256-colour SGR (38;5/48;5), truecolor SGR
(38;2/48;2), any OSC handling (OSC 8 hyperlinks print as
garbage), and the alternate screen (DECSET 47/1047/1048/1049).
It also turns blink + dark background into a bright background
in FbShell::adjustCharAttr (VGA trick); with real bright
backgrounds available that only corrupts colours - fastfetch's
black colour square came out grey - so the patch removes it.

Changes:
  vterm_action.cpp  SGR extended colours; alternate screen
                    (47/1047 swap buffer, 1048 cursor, 1049 both;
                    scrollback untouched by the alternate screen)
  vterm_states.cpp  ESC ] enters the OSC state; ESC \ = ST
  vterm.cpp         OSC bytes swallowed until BEL/CAN/SUB/ST
                    (FbTerm palette OSC ] P / ] R still works);
                    no history saves from the alternate screen
  vterm.h           ESosc state, OSC/alternate-screen members
  fbshell.cpp       blink no longer brightens the background

Parser verified with a headless VTerm harness: 40/40 checks
pass, stock parser fails 23 of the same 40.

Apply after the Debian patch series (the setup script does the
whole cycle):  patch -p1 < fbterm-compat.patch

